Downtimes
A (scheduled) downtime is a planned maintenance period. Hosts and services are handled differently by Checkmk during a downtime, for example, notifications are disabled.

Related documentation
How to use the query DSL used in the query parameters of these endpoints, have a look at the Querying Status Data section of this documentation.

These endpoints support all Livestatus filter operators, which you can look up in the Checkmk documentation.

For a detailed list of columns, please take a look at the downtimes table definition.

Relations
Downtime object can have the following relations:

self - The downtime itself.
urn:com.checkmk:rels/host_config - The host the downtime applies to.
urn:org.restfulobjects/delete - The endpoint to delete downtimes.
